cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use HyperMRI in your research, please cite it as below. When you use
  an example dataset, please also cite the dataset and its article as given in
  the documentation.
type: software
title: "HyperMRI: Python research tools for loading, reconstructing, and visualizing MRI data"
abstract: >-
  HyperMRI loads Bruker ParaVision and other MRI data, reconstructs it into
  labelled xarray objects with physical coordinates, and provides spectroscopy
  fitting, analysis and an interactive Plotly viewer for hyperpolarized and
  conventional MRI research.
authors:
  - family-names: Nagel
    given-names: Luca
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5530-6264"
  - name: HyperMRI contributors
    website: "https://github.com/LucaNagel/hypermri/blob/main/CONTRIBUTORS.md"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-27"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/LucaNagel/hypermri"
url: "https://hypermri.readthedocs.io/en/stable/"
keywords:
  - MRI
  - hyperpolarized MRI
  - Bruker
  - magnetic resonance spectroscopy
  - xarray
  - medical imaging
